, <italic>p</italic> &#x0003c; 0.001 (compared with the group of arsenicosis patients before intervention).</p></fn><fn id="tfn12-ehp0115-000659"><label>c</label><p><italic>t</italic> = 1.90, <italic>p</italic> &#x0003e; 0.05 (compared with the controls surveyed in 2004).</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap></sec><ref-list><title>References</title><ref id="b1-ehp0115-000659"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group><name><surname>An</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Hu</surname><given-names>X</given-names></name><name><surname>He</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><year>1996</year><article-title>A follow up investigation in Bazi Village thirty years after the discovery of arsenicosis</article-title><source>Chin Public Health</source><volume>12</volume><issue>7</issue><fpage>307</fpage><lpage>308</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="b2-ehp0115-000659"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group><name><surname>An</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Li</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>Control status and countermeasures of endemic arsenicosis in Guizhou Province</article-title><source>Chin J Endemiol</source><volume>24</volume><issue>2</issue><fpage>214</fpage><lpage>216</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="b3-ehp0115-000659"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group><name><surname>An</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Wang</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Hu</surname><given-names>X</given-names></name></person-group><year>2001a</year><article-title>Effect evaluation of health education in the pilot regions of Guizhou Province</article-title><source>Chin J Endemiol</source><volume>20</volume><issue>5</issue><fpage>386</fpage><lpage>387</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="b4-ehp0115-000659"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group><name><surname>An</surname><given-names>D</given